## IWindowHandle

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Models`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

### Purpose
Represents a handle to an opened browser window for lifecycle management. Returned by `IBrowserService` methods.

### Interface Definition

```csharp
public interface IWindowHandle : IDisposable
{
    event EventHandler<EventArgs>? Closing;
    bool Disposed { get; }
    void Close();
}
```

### Properties

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `Disposed` | `bool` | Whether the window has been disposed |

### Events

#### Closing
Fired when the window is closing.

```csharp
event EventHandler<EventArgs>? Closing;
```

### Methods

#### Close()
Closes the window.

```csharp
void Close();
```

#### Dispose()
Disposes the window handle and releases resources.

```csharp
void Dispose();
```

### Usage Example

```csharp
var handle = browserService.OpenUri(new Uri("https://example.com"), "Example");

// Subscribe to closing event
handle.Closing += (s, e) => Console.WriteLine("Window is closing");

// Close programmatically
handle.Close();

// Or dispose
handle.Dispose();

// Check state
if (handle.Disposed)
{
    Console.WriteLine("Window has been disposed");
}
```

### Related
